1
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Win or lose... Everyone has their fight.

2
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Never Back Down is a drama, action film directed by Jeff Wadlow.

3
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Jake, full of anger after his father's death, is just starting to find a place for himself at his new Orlando high
school - until Ryan, head of an underground MMA fight club, picks Jake out as a prime opponent.

4
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:42,000
After being trounced by Ryan in front of the entire school, Jake begins training under
the firm, moral guidance of a MMA master, where he learns how to fight...

5
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:21,000
and how to avoid a fight.

6
00:33:54,000 --> 00:34:00,000
But it becomes obvious that a rematch will be inevitable if Jake
wants to stop Ryan and his bullying, once and for all.

7
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:39,000
Jake Tyler, played by Sean Faris.

8
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:18,000
Baja Miller, played by Amber Heard.

9
00:50:51,000 --> 00:50:57,000
Ryan McCarthy, played by Cam Gigandet.

10
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Jean Roqua, played by Djimon Hounsou.

11
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:15,000
Max Cooperman, played by Evan Peters.

12
01:07:48,000 --> 01:07:54,000
Margot Tyler, played by Leslie Hope.

13
01:13:27,000 --> 01:13:33,000
Never Back Down is a 2008 American martial arts sports drama film directed
by Jeff Wadlow and starring Sean Faris and Cam Gigandet.

14
01:19:06,000 --> 01:19:12,000
It tells the story of a frustrated and conflicted teenager who arrives at a
new high school and discovers an underground fight club there.

15
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:51,000
The film was theatrically released on March 14, 2008 by Summit Entertainment.

16
01:30:24,000 --> 01:30:30,000
It received generally negative reviews from critics, though it successfully
grossed $41.6 million worldwide against a budget of $20 million.

17
01:36:03,000 --> 01:36:09,000
It was followed by a titular film series, which included three sequels.

18
01:41:42,000 --> 01:41:48,000
The film explores themes of high school, martial
arts, sports, fight, underground.

19
01:47:21,000 --> 01:47:27,000
The tone is emotional.
